7592186050730 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050762 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050762 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119906 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050762 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186119907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050762 #edb/ref 1031 "Products of Even and Odd Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050762 #edb/ref 1033 1827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050762 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "64c3046d-a138-5352-b63d-ff4dc6033ccf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050962 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050962 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048753 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050962 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115262 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050962 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186115263 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050962 #edb/ref 1031 "Horizontal Reflections of Functions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050962 #edb/ref 1033 1585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050962 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "75aea66f-2cbf-5c78-849b-d3faa857b9b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228513 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186228514 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228513 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186228515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228513 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228513 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228513 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "26b448a2-e51a-55e2-83f4-b1600db4d15b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228514 #edb/ref 1080 "even" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228514 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228514 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ae3e4430-79d1-5438-a5dc-596c25c80d7a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228515 #edb/ref 1080 "odd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228515 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228515 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "398b8812-7269-553f-be7e-33752ad3bb87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228516 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186228517 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228516 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186228518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228516 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045494 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228516 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228516 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ec05a3f8-4f27-5cb9-80b1-78194eaa18bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228517 #edb/ref 1080 "sine terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228517 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228517 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dbeb0673-168c-5f9c-93d6-d239f7912049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228518 #edb/ref 1080 "cosine terms" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228518 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228518 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e012cfa9-add7-5499-b0cf-7c9691819972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228939 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21803" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228939 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx) \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi$-periodic extensions of some functions from $x \\in [-\\pi,\\pi)$ to $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ with the Fourier series shown above.  What are the Fourier constant coefficient, the $3\\textrm{rd}$ Fourier sine coefficient, and the $8\\textrm{th}$ Fourier cosine coefficient of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228939 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cf8f2367-68af-5ef4-ac2e-5a73e37695d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228939 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ be $2\\pi$-periodic functions with Fourier series\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & ∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)), \\\\ g(x) & ∼\\frac{{c}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({c}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{d}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen for any constants $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$,\n\n$$\n\\alpha f(x) + \\beta g(x)\n\\sim\n\\frac{\\alpha a_0 + \\beta c_0}{2}\n+\n\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\n\\Big(\n(\\alpha a_n + \\beta c_n)\\cos(nx)\n+\n(\\alpha b_n + \\beta d_n)\\sin(nx)\n\\Big).\n$$\n\nUsing the linearity property of Fourier series, the corresponding Fourier coefficients of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$ are\n\n- $-3a_0+4c_0$ for the constant coefficient,\n\n- $-3a_n+4c_n,$ $n \\ge 1$ for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- $-3b_n+4d_n,$ $n \\ge 1$ for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore,\n\n- the Fourier constant coefficient of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$ is $-3a_0+4c_0$,\n\n- the $3$rd Fourier sine coefficient of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$ is $-3b_3+4d_3$, and\n\n- the $8$th Fourier cosine coefficient of $-3f(x)+4g(x)$ is $-3a_8+4c_8$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228940 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21804" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228940 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the function $f(x)=x\\cos(2x)$ on $x \\in [-\\pi,\\pi].$ Complete the statements below by filling in the blanks.\nDetermine if the function $f(x)$ is odd or even, and which terms of the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228940 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f43f5028-9314-5123-bbd8-85dc5c4a9b2b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228940 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2(-x)) \\\\  & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-2x) \\\\  & =(-x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x) = -f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi,\\pi],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\na_n=\\frac{1}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi} f(x)\\cos(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\na_0=\\frac{1}{\\pi}\\int_{-\\pi}^{\\pi} f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\cos(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\cos(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi,\\pi]$ is $0.$ Thus, $a_n=0$ for all $n\\ge1,$ and $a_0=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\text{odd}}$ and the $\\bbox[4pt, border: solid 1pt gainsboro]{\\text{cosine}}$ terms  in its Fourier series must be zero." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228941 #edb/ref 1069 "e-21805" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228941 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/23/238174bfcd0e07603a8516f9271efff876e36cf8021403be57b049ec31b60977.png)\nLet ![](images/a6/a600da93d54ed8b4857befa58c1165e8c02b77d1c2fc5b1f460961dc135c50a7.png) be the ![](images/18/1898332940848e9192873afe50ec9d9a005baf8bcb86ce77c66231321ba3fe0e.png)-periodic extension of a function from ![](images/5f/5ff1e4e25630b889a7d37b5ac7252742b9b0f0abdf659ece1f3b0700815ddc44.png) to ![](images/d3/d33b55bb712e2f8437446299936998a79ee357a6aa77ce6c31932bb464868bb8.png) with the Fourier series shown above. What is the ![](images/db/db700c8ee08453d9f4b0f347c4f88daf4186495494840905e9196b2243899653.png)th sine Fourier coefficient of ![](images/c3/c38b7489bfb362de743d5a53941eaddfc382f5d50756b13bc6a4fda893a692e9.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228941 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "848cc0af-b940-5ead-81ac-49cc6d2f4989" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186228941 #edb/ref 1074 "The Fourier series of ![](images/93/9363d37d53374519f1170d2c1c24ecb690a6810a304207ef21a0d1f3eba609de.png) is\n![](images/51/51c0039997e64ade9fb16a68ccaf87323ba205a85deb1020b5f74cd072dbf8f2.png)\n\nRecall that the corresponding Fourier coefficients of ![](images/5c/5c09997f1e5ab45e800dfc2a1fdbd766ce0e96033dd656a3128a5543bb6894a5.png) are\n\n- ![](images/fd/fdd27d69b84de936d93ebc06bc7e813d9002f40141d1d79fa787e46fc3dc4d23.png) for the constant coefficient,\n\n- ![](images/6b/6bd1cc889fa6814efed8288ad3a4be7c23fd86cd74c239ee933f770c87eb756d.png) ![](images/f5/f582369f4b0075444e7e450e4a2b92413b8f5d55be2f27222637c1eb56cddd0f.png) for the cosine coefficients, and\n\n- ![](images/23/230850b2bfeae1c1cf561825fb543c43e08e105076be3f1241f5e4590f4bf537.png) ![](images/bb/bbfce07e48b9a1eb79082aa046d29029cb6771b8243b5af1c0b9a353a5f1e379.png) for the sine coefficients.\n\nTherefore, the ![](images/16/16cfd7f94cefe4ac0dca3045d59624a00c7f962d2a2cc1138a2407db521c8800.png)th sine coefficient of ![](images/55/55bae3cc544df2d070b283a68deef7a5e53cf0f456aabd8062d0346a52662c03.png) is ![](images/92/9264ca9ad64ff750e95f9523e56c79e665af874d3b13d601018061499c64ec41.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229728 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229729 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186315013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186315014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186315015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186315016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186315017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1039 "Using Linearity of Fourier Series" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186228939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229173 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "eb295d6c-62fe-59bc-a139-49785ac98f1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229174 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229174 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050962 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229174 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229174 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186229720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229174 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186315018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229174 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186315019 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186229174 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186315020 #edb/ref 1759218604